B.ep=new A.ab(B.c9F,["Deep Garonne gravel mounds over iron-pan (alios) and sand","Fine, very chalky, stony gravel with quartz sand","Sedimentary Garonne gravel over marl bedrock","Gravel mixed with dense clay that keeps the vines cool","Quartz pebbles and gravel, sand, clay and shelly limestone","Gravel over clay-limestone and Miocene marl","Starfish-limestone plateau, white clay and iron-rich 'crasse de fer'","A dome of blue smectite clay over iron-rich 'crasse de fer'","Bajocian limestone and iron-rich Oxfordian marl","Alluvial fan of the Combe Lavaux: stony limestone and marl","Deeply fissured Bathonian limestone, thin stony soil","White Oxfordian marl and crumbly Bathonian limestone","Kimmeridgian marl full of tiny fossil oysters (Exogyra virgula)","Pure Campanian chalk at the surface, belemnites and flint nodules","Flaky mica-schist (C\xf4te Brune) and sandy limestone (C\xf4te Blonde)","Rounded Rh\xf4ne quartz pebbles over red clay and sand","'Terres blanches' (Kimmeridgian marl), 'caillottes' limestone and flint","A unique geological mosaic: granite, pink Vosges sandstone, limestone and marl","Terraces ('restanques') of very chalky clay and Triassic sandstone","Jurassic limestone scree and marl at the foot of the cliff","Clay-limestone on the Ebro's alluvial terraces, ferrous sandstone","Tertiary limestone, silty layers and plateau chalk","Brown, crusted, very free-draining limestone soils that hold water deep down","Llicorella: black and copper-tinged Palaeozoic slate","Sant'Agata marl (clay and fine sand) and Helvetian sandstone","Galestro (crumbly schist) and Alberese (compact Tuscan limestone)","The Rutherford alluvial fan: gravel beds and volcanic ash","Sandy, stony alluvium studded with pure white limestone","Deep, fertile red clay mixed with sand and iron","Vertical, fractured schist that lets roots drink 10 m down","Crumbly, chalky Campanian limestone (the 'terres blanches' of Grande Champagne)","Tawny siliceous sand and 'boulb\xe8nes', typical of Bas-Armagnac","Jurassic clay-limestone marl and flint in the Normandy valleys","Urgonian limestone of the Pre-Alps and mountain forests","White Senonian chalk cliffs of the Pays de Caux","Thick, waterlogged peat bogs, heather and Precambrian quartz","Caledonian granite bedrock and glacial alluvium of the River Spey","Grassy limestone plains and Irish alluvial peat","Ordovician limestone plateau filtering iron-free spring water","Rich, fertile volcanic andosols of Mount Pel\xe9e","Red volcanic soils rich in iron and minerals from the Tequila volcano","The Thames alluvial basin and pure water springs","Fertile chernozem plains and sandy-silty soils for fine cereals","Temperate oceanic, moderated by the Gironde estuary","Mild, temperate oceanic","Protective maritime oceanic","Northern maritime oceanic","Oceanic, softened by the Landes forest","A unique misty morning microclimate, born where the Ciron meets the Garonne","Oceanic with a marked continental influence","Temperate oceanic turning continental","Semi-continental, with cool nights and hot summers","Northern semi-continental","Semi-continental, tempered by the Combe d'Ambin","Sunny semi-continental","Cool semi-continental, exposed to spring frosts","Both oceanic and cold continental influences","Temperate continental, swept by the north wind (Mistral)","Hot and very dry Mediterranean, kept healthy by a strong Mistral","Degraded oceanic with a continental tone","Very sheltered, dry semi-continental (Vosges foehn effect)","Maritime Mediterranean with over 3,000 hours of sun a year","Upland Mediterranean with wide day/night temperature swings","Continental, tempered by the Atlantic influence of the Sierra Cantabria","Extreme continental: harsh winters and scorching summers with cool nights","Semi-arid Mediterranean with over 300 days of sun","Arid mountain Mediterranean","Temperate continental with legendary autumn fogs (nebbia)","Hot Mediterranean, tempered by the Tyrrhenian sea breeze","Mediterranean, tempered by morning fogs from San Pablo Bay","High-altitude desert (constant sun and Andean glacier meltwater)","Hot, sunny Mediterranean","Very dry, torrid Mediterranean, sheltered by the Serra do Mar\xe3o","Mild, temperate and humid oceanic, generous to the angels' share","Temperate sub-Atlantic, under Pyrenean and oceanic influence","Humid, mild, temperate oceanic, ideal for orchards","Harsh Alpine, tempered by the valleys","Bracing oceanic, swept by Channel winds","Wild, rainy oceanic, swept by Atlantic spray","Temperate sub-polar oceanic, crystal-clear spring water from the Cairngorms","Mild, temperate oceanic with heavy rainfall","Humid continental with extreme seasonal temperature swings","Hot, humid maritime tropical, paced by the trade winds","Semi-arid subtropical with clear dry and rainy seasons","Temperate maritime oceanic","Temperate continental with icy winters","Gentle slopes facing east / south-east towards the river","Gently rolling mounds facing the river","A plateau sloping slightly east","Slopes along the Gironde estuary","Well-drained gravel mounds","North / north-east-facing slopes sheltered from the wind","A natural amphitheatre facing due south","A gentle plateau topping out at 40 metres","A steep slope facing due east","East and south-east hillsides","Due east, catching the sun from dawn","East and south-east, mid-slope","A steep south-west-facing slope above the Serein","Chalk cliff facing due east","Dizzying slopes terraced into 'cheys', up to 60%, facing south-east","Open, sun-drenched plateaus and terraces","A rocky spur and steep hills above the Loire","Steep slopes facing east to south-east","A natural amphitheatre opening onto the Mediterranean","South and east foothills of the limestone massif","South-facing terraces and slopes","Arid plateaus and slopes along the Douro river","High plateaus and valleys ringed by mountains","'Costers' (dizzying slopes up to 50%) in terraces","Winding south-facing slopes ('sor\xec')","Gentle Tuscan hills facing Monte Amiata","Valley floor and slopes of the Mayacamas and Vaca ranges","Andean foothills below Mount Tupungato","A rolling valley sheltered by the Barossa Ranges","Dizzyingly steep terraces ('socalcos' and 'patamares')","Open, rolling slopes along the Charente river","Gentle slopes wooded with Gascon pedunculate oak","Traditional grassy, grazed standard-tree orchards","Alpine slopes sheltered in the Is\xe8re valley","The maritime valley of F\xe9camp, open to the coast","Wild shores of Loch Indaal and the Sound of Islay","Sheltered Spey glens lined with Caledonian pine forest","Green, temperate coastal valleys, south and north","Rolling Bluegrass hills and the Kentucky River valleys","Volcanic slopes and sunny sugar-cane plains","Arid plateaus and volcanic slopes below the Tequila volcano","The historic heart of British urban distilling","The great cereal plateaus of Central Europe","12 - 30 m","10 - 24 m","15 - 22 m","14 - 28 m","25 - 60 m","30 - 80 m","40 - 100 m","25 - 42 m","250 - 310 m","260 - 380 m","250 - 350 m","230 - 320 m","130 - 250 m","120 - 240 m","180 - 340 m","40 - 120 m","150 - 310 m","200 - 450 m","50 - 250 m","150 - 400 m","400 - 700 m","720 - 880 m (high-altitude vineyard)","400 - 900 m","300 - 750 m","250 - 450 m","200 - 550 m","50 - 450 m","900 - 1450 m (very high vineyard)","250 - 400 m","100 - 600 m","20 - 160 m","80 - 200 m","40 - 150 m","280 - 1000 m","10 - 80 m","0 - 150 m","150 - 500 m","20 - 120 m","150 - 300 m","20 - 450 m","1200 - 2100 m (high altitude)","15 - 40 m","Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot (a high share)","Syrah (dominant), co-fermented with up to 20% Viognier","Grenache Noir (dominant), Mourv\xe8dre, Syrah, Cinsault (13 permitted grapes)","Mourv\xe8dre (at least 50% in the reds), Grenache, Cinsault","Tinto Fino (local Tempranillo, 95%), Cabernet Sauvignon","Monastrell (Mourv\xe8dre, 80%), Syrah, Garnacha Tintorera","Garnacha Peluda, Cari\xf1ena (century-old Carignan), Syrah","Sangiovese Grosso (Brunello, 100%)","Shiraz (century-old, pre-phylloxera vines), Cabernet Sauvignon, Grenache","Bittersweet (Bisquet, B\xe9dan) and sharp cider apples, pears","Grain spirit infused and distilled with 130 Alpine plants and herbs","27 plants and spices from around the world (angelica, hyssop, saffron, juniper, cinnamon)","Malted barley dried over local peat smoke","100% malted barley (unpeated or lightly toasted malt)","Malted and unmalted raw barley (single pot still)","At least 51% yellow corn, rye, malted barley, wheat","Fresh pressed sugar-cane juice (unrefined 'vesou')","100% Agave Tequilana Weber, blue variety (agave hearts, 'pi\xf1as')","Neutral spirit redistilled with juniper berries (Juniperus communis), coriander, angelica, citrus","Dankowskie golden rye, soft winter wheat, Stobrawa potatoes","First Growths, 1855 classification (Latour, Lafite, Mouton)","First Growth, 1855 classification (Ch\xe2teau Margaux)","Classified Growths, 1855 (L\xe9oville, Ducru-Beaucaillou)","Second Growths (Cos d'Estournel, Montrose)","Graves Classified Growth (Ch\xe2teau Haut-Brion, 1855)","Superior First Growth, 1855 (Ch\xe2teau d'Yquem)","Premiers Grands Crus Class\xe9s A (Figeac, Pavie \u2014 2022 classification)","An elite village appellation (Petrus, Le Pin, Lafleur)","Grands Crus (Roman\xe9e-Conti and La T\xe2che, monopoles; Richebourg)","7 Chablis Grand Cru 'climats' (Les Clos, Valmur, Vaud\xe9sir)","17 villages rated 100% Grand Cru","Northern Rh\xf4ne cru appellations (C\xf4te-R\xf4tie, Hermitage, Cornas, Condrieu)","A pioneer of French appellations (AOC 1936)","Centre-Loire appellations","51 Alsace Grand Cru terroirs","Provence's leading cru (AOC 1941)","A Languedoc cru (village appellation)","A UNESCO World Heritage vineyard","AOC Cognac (Grande Champagne / Petite Champagne crus)","AOC Calvados Pays d'Auge (double distillation)","A historic monastic liqueur (1605 manuscript)","A monastic elixir born, legend has it, in 1510","GI Irish Whiskey (triple distillation)","AOC Rhum de Martinique (the world's only rum AOC)","Denominaci\xf3n de Origen Tequila (CRT certified)","EU regulatory category: London Dry Gin","The poor, free-draining gravel forces the vine to send its roots down as far as 6 metres for water, giving the wines a regal tannic structure and decades of ageing potential.","The finest gravel in the M\xe9doc gives inimitably silky tannins and a delicate floral bouquet of violet and cedar.","The M\xe9doc's perfect balance: the power and structure of Pauillac wed to the elegance and finesse of Margaux.","The clay subsoils bring mineral freshness and a compact frame that stands up brilliantly to hot vintages.","The historic cradle of Bordeaux wine since Roman times. Legendary smoky minerality, in red and white alike.","Morning mists encourage Botrytis cinerea (noble rot), while warm afternoons concentrate the sugars and the aromas of candied apricot and saffron.","The starfish-limestone bedrock acts as a sponge that regulates water, giving Merlot a velvety opulence and a vibrant limestone freshness.","Petrus's legendary dome of blue clay holds moisture and gives the wines a silky texture, black truffle and unmatched aromatic intensity.","The jewel of the C\xf4te d'Or. An aristocratic balance of floral lace (faded rose, peony), oriental spice and incomparable mineral tension.","The 'King of Wines'. Vigour, muscular power, firm tannins and aromas of wild black cherry, liquorice and forest floor.","The quintessence of delicacy. Called 'the silkiest wine of Burgundy', with an airy grace.","The world summit of dry white wine. Scalpel-sharp minerality, aromas of toasted hazelnut, struck flint and noble butteriness.","The iodine imprint of the ancient Jurassic sea gives the wine crystalline purity, mineral salinity and electric freshness.","The porous chalk regulates heat and water perfectly, bringing fine bubbles, crushed chalk and a remarkable saline length.","The dizzying terraces above the Rh\xf4ne catch the sun's heat. Syrah gives off notes of black olive, smoked bacon, violet and white pepper.","The rounded pebbles store the sun's heat by day and give it back to the grapes at night, taking Grenache to a fleshy, spicy, garrigue-scented fullness.","The flint soils give that famous 'gunflint' touch and grapefruit zest, while the 'caillottes' bring freshness and lace.","The Vosges barrier shelters the vineyards, creating one of the driest regions in France, where Riesling shows chiselled, rocky minerality.","Mourv\xe8dre's sacred ground, with its feet in the sea. Wines for ageing, with notes of fine leather, black cherry, Mediterranean undergrowth and spice.","Cool air flowing down from the causse at night keeps an aromatic freshness and a tannic finesse that stand out in the southern heat.","Oak barrels and slow ripening give Tempranillo its signature aromas of vanilla, leather, blond tobacco and macerated red fruit.","The extreme altitude keeps a vibrant acidity despite the formidable sun-driven concentration of black berries and liquorice.","The kingdom of old, ungrafted Monastrell vines. Concentrated candied black fruit, wild garrigue and a chocolatey finish.","Llicorella slate gives tiny yields (10 hl/ha) and wines of stunning mineral, smoky, graphite intensity.","Nebbiolo gives its translucent garnet brilliance here, with aromas of noble tar, dried rose petal, white truffle and masterful acidity.","On galestro, Sangiovese finds its noblest expression: morello cherry, black tea, Russian leather and dense, vibrant tannins.","The famous 'Rutherford dust'. Rich, opulent Cabernets with notes of ripe blackcurrant, mocha, cedar and velvety, very fine-grained tannins.","Intense UV light thickens Malbec's skins while icy Andean nights lock in acidity, making deep purple wines with notes of blueberry and violet.","Some of the world's oldest ungrafted Shiraz vines (planted in 1843). Jammy black fruit, prune, eucalyptus and dark chocolate.","One of the world's oldest demarcated regions (1756). A heroic terroir, carved by hand, making great vintage Ports and superb dry wines.","Double distillation in the copper Charentais still, then long ageing in French Limousin oak, developing the legendary 'rancio'.","France's oldest brandy (1310). Continuous distillation in the Armagnac still and ageing in black Gascon oak: a rustic, powerful brandy with notes of prune, vanilla and spice.","Distilled from pure-juice Normandy cider and aged in oak. Intense aromas of butter-roasted apple, tarte Tatin, salted-butter caramel and sweet spice.","Said to be the only liqueur that keeps ageing and improving in the bottle for decades. A complex herbal symphony of peppermint, anise, wild thyme, g\xe9n\xe9pi and saffron.","Quadruple distillation in hammered copper stills from 1888 and ageing in century-old oak casks. Silky texture, spiced honey, candied orange peel and oriental notes.","The world's sanctuary of peated, iodine-laden whiskies. Intense notes of wood smoke, medicinal tar, salty seaweed, oyster and wild peat, softened by Bourbon or Sherry casks.","The historic, prestigious heart of Scotch whisky. Elegance, roundness, honeyed notes of green apple, ripe pear, toasted malt, vanilla and lavish Oloroso Sherry casks.","The tradition of triple pot-still distillation gives an incomparable buttery smoothness, with no smoky edge, and notes of baking spice, yellow peach, fudge and fine wood.","Kentucky's scorching summers and icy winters make the new, charred American oak barrels (char #4) breathe, drawing out powerful aromas of vanilla, caramel, maple, toasted corn and leather.","Unlike industrial molasses rums, agricole rum is distilled from fresh cane juice. An aromatic burst of fresh cane, lime zest and white flowers when young, noble vanilla oak when aged.","Blue agave pi\xf1as ripen 7 to 10 years under the Mexican sun before slow cooking in masonry ovens. Fresh green aromas, white pepper, candied agave, wild herbs and volcanic minerality.","Pure distillation, with no flavouring or sugar added after the still. Resinous, piquant juniper up front, fresh lemon zest, orris root and coriander seed.","Absolute purity from multiple column distillations and charcoal filtration. Oily, creamy texture, notes of fresh rye bread, soft vanilla and delicate white pepper.","Northern Rh\xf4ne Valley (C\xf4te-R\xf4tie & Hermitage)","Ch\xe2teauneuf-du-Pape & Southern Rh\xf4ne","Douro Valley (Cima Corgo)","Chartreuse, the Carthusian liqueur (Voiron)","Martinique & Caribbean Agricole Rum","Agave Tequila & Mezcal (Jalisco & Oaxaca)","Traditional Vodka (Rye, Wheat & Potato)"],t.l)
